      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T15:45:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The console is defined in each separate `board/\u003cboardname\u003e/ec.tasklist` (for example [board/bloonchipper/ec.tasklist](http://cs/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/board/hatch_fp/ec.tasklist;l\u003d9) and looks like this:\n```\n#define CONFIG_TASK_LIST \\\n\tTASK_ALWAYS_RO(RWSIG, rwsig_task, NULL, 1280) \\\n\tTASK_ALWAYS(HOOKS, hook_task, NULL, 1024) \\\n\tTASK_ALWAYS_RW(FPSENSOR, fp_task, NULL, 4096) \\\n\tTASK_ALWAYS(HOSTCMD, host_command_task, NULL, 4096) \\\n\tTASK_ALWAYS(CONSOLE, console_task, NULL, CONSOLE_TASK_STACK_SIZE)\n```\nand `CONSOLE_TASK_STACK_SIZE` is defined per chip, such as for [stm32](http://cs/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/chip/stm32/config_chip.h?rcl\u003d71b2ef709dcb14260f5fdaa3ab4ced005a29fb46\u0026l\u003d129). \n\nI believe that it would be possible to change the `CONSOLE` task definition to \n`TASK_NOTEST(CONSOLE, console_task, NULL, CONSOLE_TASK_STACK_SIZE)` to get the default console task for standard builds and add a separate `TASK_TEST(CONSOLE, console_task, NULL, CONSOLE_TEST_TASK_STACK_SIZE)` to each `\u003ctestname\u003e.tasklist` file. However, I _think_ this would require updating all boards and tests (although many are symlinks) and I\u0027m worried that this might be error prone.\n\nLooking back now I agree that my method may not be the cleanest / most obvious solution. Maybe it\u0027s cleaner to create a config flag such as `CONFIG_CONSOLE_TASK_STACK_SIZE` or `CONFIG_USE_LARGE_CONSOLE_TASK_STACK` since is consistent with the infrastructure already in place and there is already [some precedent](http://cs/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/include/shimmed_task_id.h?l\u003d65).",
      "parentUuid": "d1a6c74e_5bcc5218",
